get.description:
Returns the org's person grants, newest first. The optional
status filter (active|suspended|revoked|all) narrows the list;
an unknown filter is a 400, never a widened list.

installed_sha.description:
InstalledSHA / NextSHA are the review's two pinned commits;
NextDigest is the NEXT compile's pin (the apply target's digest —
Ref.Digest is the compiled-bytes hash, never an image digest).

source.description:
Source / Target name the clone's two scopes. The InstallRef's
ProjectID + ClusterID are the scope key (the engine identity);
InstallName is empty on both — the plan covers the whole scope.

runId.description:
RunID is GitHub's workflow run id (0 for the BMC-run sources);
LogSize the capture's COMPRESSED byte size (0 until captured);
Hosted true only for github rows.

workflow.description:
Workflow stays empty in v1 — GitHub's workflow name has no
delivering story yet (the events feed carries actions only);
surfaced when a story owns it.

absolute_max_expires_at.description:
AbsoluteMaxExpiresAt is the hard cap for sliding-mode grants. Nullable;
meaningful only when ExpirationMode == "sliding". No amount of activity
extends a grant past this time (NFR4 — no uncapped sliding).

